              "item": {
                "@type": "PodcastEpisode",
                "@id": "https://www.mikeye.com/podcast/the-window-opens-before-it-is-obvious#episode",
                "name": "The Window Opens Before It Is Obvious",
                "url": "https://www.mikeye.com/podcast/the-window-opens-before-it-is-obvious",
                "description": "Episode 6 of The Mike Ye Briefing explores timing asymmetry: whether waiting creates more optionality or quietly takes options away. Mike Ye draws on the Express divestiture as fast fashion emerged, Intel Capital's monetization of more than $5 billion across over 200 investments before the dot-com bubble fully burst, and Penske Media's early relationship with South by Southwest following the Covid shutdown. The episode examines why good timing is sometimes judgment, sometimes luck, and most valuable when preparation allows action before the window becomes obvious.",
                "episodeNumber": 6,
                "datePublished": "2026-08-26",
                "inLanguage": "en-US",
                "partOfSeries": {
